{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TrillionniumFoundation/Trillionnium-Chain/pulls/847","id":5225636007,"node_id":"PR_kwDOTty1_c8AAAABN3jgpw","html_url":"https://github.com/TrillionniumFoundation/Trillionnium-Chain/pull/847","diff_url":"https://github.com/TrillionniumFoundation/Trillionnium-Chain/pull/847.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/TrillionniumFoundation/Trillionnium-Chain/pull/847.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TrillionniumFoundation/Trillionnium-Chain/issues/847","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TrillionniumFoundation/Trillionnium-Chain/pulls/847/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TrillionniumFoundation/Trillionnium-Chain/pulls/847/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TrillionniumFoundation/Trillionnium-Chain/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TrillionniumFoundation/Trillionnium-Chain/issues/847/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TrillionniumFoundation/Trillionnium-Chain/statuses/2a86462a1ab20c68151719ba4635e3c294391e64","number":847,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Consolidate audited branch history and current runtime","user":{"login":"ProfHepta","id":102159240,"node_id":"U_kgDOBhbTiA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/102159240?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ProfHepta","html_url":"https://github.com/ProfHepta","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ProfHepta/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ProfHepta/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ProfHepta/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ProfHepta/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ProfHepta/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ProfHepta/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ProfHepta/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ProfHepta/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ProfHepta/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Purpose and reviewed scope\n\nThe frozen pre-consolidation inventory contains **908 branch names and 892 distinct tips**. This PR combines the selected current implementation and its original controls, records **296 terminal dispositions covering all 908 names**, and preserves the original history before branch cleanup.\n\nThe selected runtime includes ownership and lifecycle boundaries, fresh Host observation, receiver scheduling, worker accounting, native statement and mining-time controls, and the explicitly retained Cell, network and recovery APIs. Conflicting historical alternatives retain explicit dispositions; archiving an alternative is not a claim that its behavior is implemented by the current runtime.\n\nThe [audit report](https://github.com/TrillionniumFoundation/Trillionnium-Chain/blob/2a86462a1ab20c68151719ba4635e3c294391e64/docs/development/BRANCH_CONSOLIDATION_AUDIT_20261114.md), [original audit evidence index](https://github.com/TrillionniumFoundation/Trillionnium-Chain/blob/2a86462a1ab20c68151719ba4635e3c294391e64/evidence/branch-consolidation-20261114/ARTIFACT_INDEX.json) and [later execution records](https://github.com/TrillionniumFoundation/Trillionnium-Chain/blob/0f4b8b70bde65f84139b4cc7ed9e176ed55cf1d9/metadata/execution-manifest.json) distinguish source review, component observations, exact full-lane results and unresolved qualification. Current-source binding and fixture repairs retain their original acceptance limits and historical evidence.\n\n## Exact candidate and evidence\n\nCandidate: `2a86462a1ab20c68151719ba4635e3c294391e64`  \nTree: `5c26776f96f15fd131e85a5c2d7c5e895ad7fab4`  \nReviewed main base: `dd6e1c3cbeacbdc532b0679297835b3a0aac78f0`\n\n[Confirmed published source and evidence manifest](https://github.com/TrillionniumFoundation/Trillionnium-Chain/blob/0f4b8b70bde65f84139b4cc7ed9e176ed55cf1d9/metadata/archive-file-index.json). The terminal publication receipt is retained separately; it is not embedded in its own archive. Every result below must name this candidate; prospective-merge evidence must also name the reviewed main base.\n\n| Required observation | Recorded state | Original evidence |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Seven local prepublication source gates | Passed on this exact candidate (seven original commands) | [Receipt and all original outputs](https://github.com/TrillionniumFoundation/Trillionnium-Chain/blob/0f4b8b70bde65f84139b4cc7ed9e176ed55cf1d9/metadata/local-gates.json) |\n| Original full Linux `repository-truth` lane | Passed on this exact candidate (original complete fail-fast lane) | [Full fail-fast lane and source readbacks](https://github.com/TrillionniumFoundation/Trillionnium-Chain/blob/0f4b8b70bde65f84139b4cc7ed9e176ed55cf1d9/metadata/rog-full-lane.json) |\n| Required hosted checks on the exact head | Not established by this preparation; required checks remain mandatory | [Head checks](https://github.com/TrillionniumFoundation/Trillionnium-Chain/pull/847/checks) |\n| Required hosted checks on the exact prospective merge | Not established by this preparation; required checks remain mandatory | [Prospective-merge checks](https://github.com/TrillionniumFoundation/Trillionnium-Chain/pull/847/checks) |\n\nHosted status observed at: `Not supplied for this final candidate/base; no hosted pass asserted`. Missing, queued, running, failed, cancelled or timed-out results do not count as passes.\n\nThe seven source gates are project preflight, source verification before and after, repository check, generated inventory check, CI contract and PQ corpus check. Named component tests and the separate 122-command diagnostic do not substitute for the original complete Linux lane. A source-consistent result does not grant hosted or system qualification.\n\n## Preserved failures and follow-up repairs\n\nThe original public `CONFIRMATION_TARGET` failures remain failures. The **4-second window and 16 pressure workers** are unchanged; source-map reconciliation does not establish that this runtime deadline has been met.\n\nThe full local run on `dc42ce4d` stopped at the stale lifetime source lock; the later full run on `7d8d4c59` stopped at the hash-use source map. Both original outcomes and raw streams are retained. Subsequent metadata-only binding repairs are manually reviewed against their declared source inputs; their local controls are not relabelled as successful full-lane or hosted runs.\n\n**Historical collector disposition:** B1 now binds the archived collector to historical commit e4abb172147e941b62483652b0ceabaae4317624, tree 016ebf3deeac88d6d7a782edf563f2291ebe17f5 and raw SHA256 f40c5d621454d0532141920724a3cfd57e240f4a3b061536162313daa676c254. The .py.raw fixture is data only and is never executed. All 25 original bridge test methods are unchanged; six added controls bring the component result to 31 passes. Separately, the full M4 Linux lane exposed a real closed-exec-gate cleanup race (root return code -15 instead of 125). C5 preserves the 14 original collector tests, adds two deterministic controls, and defers only SIGTERM for the unreleased root after confirmed gate closure; the original kill escalation and cleanup deadline remain. The exact final full-lane result is reported independently in the table above; these component facts do not grant hosted or system qualification. ([separate reviewed disposition](https://github.com/TrillionniumFoundation/Trillionnium-Chain/blob/0f4b8b70bde65f84139b4cc7ed9e176ed55cf1d9/payload/post-m5-root-closures/reviewed-collector-disposition-v1.txt)).\n\nThat separate collector issue is not deemed repaired by the source-map changes above. Its retained historical results must not be rewritten as observations of the final candidate.\n\n## Original system acceptance conditions remain\n\n**Prior system qualification remains `HOLD_NO_GO / DENY_ALL`.** The retained original `0746` campaigns remain **0/3 passing and 0/9 phases passing**. History preservation, source checks, component tests and PR readiness do not waive the original system conditions.\n\nThe original **4-second Host service**, independent **30-second campaign**, and separate **History/capacity/churn** criteria require exact-source hosted evidence under their original contracts. The storage campaign still requires **at least three independently administered failure domains and at least 72 hours**. Failed or missing lanes remain open until their complete outcomes are collected.\n\nOrdinary Hepta daemon stage-owner assembly and the **same-operation training/evaluation/Selection-or-NoUpdate/install/FinalUse/next-task/cold-recovery trace** remain subject to the original identity, ownership and recovery requirements. Test ELFs do not supply the ordinary-daemon binary, model, loader or evaluator identities.\n\nLarge-model BT with complete custody, independent WAN operators and failure domains, real payments and sustained leases, and the required long-run deployments retain their original contracts. The PoN cost/consensus and PQ proof obligations remain conditional or unresolved. **No acceptance deadline, threshold or denominator is waived, and no production activation is granted.**\n\n## History retention and remaining repository actions\n\nRecorded history tag: `archive/execution-receipts-20261114-2a86462a1ab2-v1`  \nAnnotated tag object: `454761ef276433740453b5b80ce886c1d251c6d3`  \n[Archive commit and exact manifests](https://github.com/TrillionniumFoundation/Trillionnium-Chain/tree/0f4b8b70bde65f84139b4cc7ed9e176ed55cf1d9): `0f4b8b70bde65f84139b4cc7ed9e176ed55cf1d9`  \nCandidate explicitly captured by that archive: `2a86462a1ab20c68151719ba4635e3c294391e64`\n\nThe verified archive scope must retain all **892 original tips**, their reachable history and the exact 908-name manifest. The archive's captured candidate is stated separately from the final PR head; an older archive is not presented as containing later source or execution results. History retention does not assert semantic equivalence between alternatives or that every archived tip becomes an ancestor of linear main.\n\nMain integration must use the protected linear merge route after the required exact-head and prospective-merge acceptance checks. Branch cleanup follows a verified merge and a fresh complete reference inventory. The observed protection on `fix/chain-bulk-state-tree-20261017` disallows deletion; that remains a distinct blocker to a one-branch result, and this update does not change protection.\n\nThe audit report also retains the unresolved macOS physical-retention observation and the 27 historical dependency registry/yank-query timeouts. Main integration and final branch cleanup are not completed by this PR metadata update.\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-11-09T14:37:45Z","updated_at":"2026-11-14T14:23:10Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"a7ee9542d10e15bba4256de9579a0196ba9ab9c9","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"TrillionniumFoundation:fix/chain-hepta-closure-candidate-20261109-481716","ref":"fix/chain-hepta-closure-candidate-20261109-481716","repo":{"id":1323087357,"node_id":"R_kgDOTty1_Q","name":"Trillionnium-Chain","full_name":"TrillionniumFoundation/Trillionnium-Chain","owner":{"login":"TrillionniumFoundation","id":262513357,"node_id":"O_kgDOD6WizQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/262513357?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TrillionniumFoundation","html_url":"https://github.com/TrillionniumFoundation","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TrillionniumFoundation/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TrillionniumFoundation/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TrillionniumFoundation/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.g